    "summary": "Bookings went up, but so did cancellations: the banner rushes guests into bookings they regret.",
    "explanation": "The primary metric is a real win: +8.1% (95% CI +4.0% to +12.2%, p < 0.001), on both platforms and with a healthy split. But the guardrail exists for exactly this case. Cancellations within 48 hours rose 39.2%. Each cancelled booking costs the host a blocked calendar and Stayloop a refund and a support contact, so net bookings and trust grow much less than the headline suggests. A guardrail breach means you do not ship as is, even with a significant win on the primary metric.",
    "issueNotes": {
      "guardrail": "Cancellations within 48 hours rose 39.2% (p < 0.001), far beyond the 5% the team accepts. Many of the extra bookings come from guests rushed into dates they cancel days later."
    },
    "recommendation": "Do not ship this version. Keep urgency only when it is true and specific (real availability, no countdown), make net bookings after cancellations the primary metric, and test again.",
